menu "MicClicker C3"

choice MICCLICKER_C3_ROLE
    prompt "C3 firmware role"
    default MICCLICKER_ROLE_AUDIO_LINK

config MICCLICKER_ROLE_AUDIO_LINK
    bool "Audio link (capture, G.722 encode, ESP-NOW send)"
    help
        The stage-4 product role: capture 16 kHz mono from the ES8311, encode one
        20 ms G.722 frame per ESP-NOW packet, and send it to the bound S3 peer over
        encrypted unicast. Pairs on first boot when no binding exists.

config MICCLICKER_ROLE_SELFTEST
    bool "Hardware selftest (Wi-Fi scan, ADC buttons, G.722 vector)"
    help
        The stage-1 selftest: scans Wi-Fi, then prompts for the four button states and
        reports ADC voltages. Needs a human at the device. It does not touch the codec,
        the radio link or NVS bindings.

config MICCLICKER_ESPNOW_PROBE_SENDER
    bool "ESP-NOW probe sender (stage 3 measurement)"
    help
        The stage-3 probe: discovery, burst audio, paced audio, key retransmission,
        pairing and an encrypted round trip. Erases any stored binding on every boot,
        which product roles must never do. Selected by `./firmware/build.sh c3 --probe`.

endchoice

config MICCLICKER_ESPNOW_PROBE_CHANNEL
    int "ESP-NOW probe channel (2.4 GHz)"
    range 1 13
    default 1
    depends on MICCLICKER_ESPNOW_PROBE_SENDER
    help
        Both ends must use the same channel. The probe logs the channel it actually
        reached, so a mismatch shows up in the logs rather than only as silence.

config MICCLICKER_PAIR_ON_BOOT
    bool "Open a pairing window on boot when no binding is stored"
    default y
    depends on MICCLICKER_ROLE_AUDIO_LINK
    help
        When no pairing record exists, the C3 broadcasts one pairing request window at
        boot. Disable to require an explicit pairing gesture instead; with this off and
        no binding the device captures and encodes but never sends, which is useful for
        measuring the sender alone.

endmenu
